  "title": "Erdős Problem #32",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Is there a set $A\\subset\\mathbb{N}$ such that $ \\lvert A\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}\\rvert = o((\\log N)^2) $ and such that every large integer can be written as $p+a$ for some prime $p$ and $a\\in A$?\nCan the bound $O(\\log N)$ be achieved? Must such an $A$ satisfy $ \\liminf \\frac{\\lvert A\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}\\rvert}{\\log N}> 1? $ ",
